# The previous site was four pages; this one is a scroll journey plus a reference page. These keep
# whatever ranking and inbound links those URLs have earned, and stop Google serving 404s for paths
# it already has indexed. 301 because the move is permanent.
#
# Netlify syntax, and Cloudflare Pages reads the same file. THE SITE CURRENTLY DEPLOYS TO VERCEL,
# which ignores this file entirely: the live equivalents are in vercel.json at the repo root, and
# the two have to be changed together. On Apache convert to RewriteRule with [R=301,L].

/services      /#services      301
/services/     /#services      301
/about         /#about         301
/about/        /#about         301
/contact       /#contact       301
/contact/      /#contact       301

# /faq is a real second document, not a client-side route. This has to sit above the catch-all
# below, which would otherwise rewrite it to the home page and lose the URL entirely.
#
# The canonical form is /faq/, because the build emits faq/index.html and every static host serves
# a directory index at the trailing slash. The bare /faq is redirected to it rather than served at
# both, so there is one URL rather than two competing for the same content.
/faq           /faq/           301

# The legal documents, same reasoning: real files under a directory index, canonical with the
# trailing slash. Kept in step with `legalDocs` in src/content/legal.ts.
/privacy        /privacy/        301
/cookies        /cookies/        301
/terms          /terms/          301
/accessibility  /accessibility/  301

# Anything else resolves to the home document rather than a 404.
/*             /index.html     200
